WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.069
 Steve, Nick, congratulations.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.938
The strength of your work,
coupled with your competitors'

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.607
failures to perform, have
secured you both a place

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:11.077
in the third round, where we
will send you home to recreate

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.279
an iconic blade from history.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.947
Are you ready to see
what that weapon is?

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:15.715
 Yes, I am.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.515
 Oh, yeah.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:17.483
Yeah.

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:22.555
 Your final challenge
is deerhorn knives.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.425
 Whoa.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.094
NARRATOR: Deerhorn knives
are distinctive double-bladed

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.263
weapons, used as an
extension of the body

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:31.931
to counter and disarm opponents.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:34.100
The knives are unique
to the 19th century

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:35.968
martial art form Bagua Zhang.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.503
Students of this
discipline train

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.973
with the weapon in both
hands to master techniques

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.374
in slashing and seizing.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.910
Easily concealed in
traditional Chinese garb,

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.212
these mighty knives can
be swiftly brandished

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.716
to catch an opponent off-guard
and deliver deadly cuts

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.417
with four horn-shaped points.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:53.986
The weapons are notably
employed in the film

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.455
"Crouching Tiger,
Hidden Dragon."

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.391
 I've never heard
of a deerhorn knife.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.393 line:0%
It's definitely not a
design I'm familiar with.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.165 line:0%
 I was hoping for a
fairly simple sword.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.333 line:7%
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.370 line:7%
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.672 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:17.210
 Today I start
the deerhorn knife.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:20.346
I want to make this thing
look like deer antlers.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.448
I'm used to making
straight pieces.

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:25.251
This thing has curves
all over the place.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.420
And I have to make
two of these things.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:33.059
Now I have to figure out how I'm
going to make this out of this.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.560
[music playing]

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.196
I want to forge this out
of one piece of steel

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.432
because that's the
strongest way you can do it.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:43.236
I'm going to cut a slit down
the center of this bar, spread

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.071
the handle and the
front blade apart,

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:47.774
and hopefully it all
is going to go to plan.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.343
[tools whirring]

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:53.479 line:0%
That looks a lot more
like a deer antler.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.283 line:0%
 Day two, well, I've
decided to do a butt weld.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.087
I'm cutting the crescents
apart and welding it flat on.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.522
So now the edges will line up.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.722
It looks very nice.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.859
Ready to do the heat treat.
(HIGH-PITCHED VOICE) No, no.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.493
I don't want to go
in the fire again.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.261
No!

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.265
My only concern right now
is if this weird shape

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:17.670
decides to warp at all,
it could be a problem.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.440
In to quench.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:23.809
[music playing]

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:26.846
There we go.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.347
That is as hard as a file.

00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:30.049
They didn't warp into a pretzel.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:33.285 line:7%
So, hey, I'm great.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:36.221 line:0%
 Day four, I've got both
of these weapons shaped.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.690
It's time to harden them.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.824
This is the moment.

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:40.026
This has to work.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.929
If it doesn't, I'm not
going to have a weapon.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.899
[sizzling]

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.834
Hey, no warp-age.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.968
Let's see if we got hardened.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.470
[clanging]

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.705
It worked.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.740
I feel really great.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.109
I'm grinding the bevels.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.844
Everything is coming together.

00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:00.580
And then I see it.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.682
Uh oh.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.984
I've got a crack in
one of my blades.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:05.985
That's heartbreaking.

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.519
It's going through both ends.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.855
And there's nothing
I can do about it.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.990
I've got to test it.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.526
[thudding]

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.360
I need a pole of some kind.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.965
I know they're going to
do something like this.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:22.435
[music playing]

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.838
[thudding]

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.373
[clatter]

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.475 line:7%
[sighs]

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.144 line:7%
 Day five, I feel like crap.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.813
If it wasn't for the
fact that I'm sick,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.582
I actually kind of like
this deep, gravelly voice.

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:38.984
If I didn't have to hack
up my lung to do it,

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.519
I'd have it all the time.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.755
All I have left to
do is put the handles

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.490
on and sharpen the blades.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.360
Putting the handles on
is shaping the material

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.562
a little bit, gluing
them on, drilling

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:51.830
holes, and putting
the pins in place

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.332
to hold everything together.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.434 line:7%
That's all ready to go.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.137 line:0%
 It's day five, and
I have to start over.

00:03:58.203 --> 00:04:01.407
I've got one day to
build a pair of these.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:05.578
I don't know if I'm going
to be able to do it or not.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:09.415
If I wasn't the underdog
before, I definitely am now.

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:11.617
I just want to have
something to take there.

00:04:11.683 --> 00:04:15.487
I have three days of
work to do in 10 hours.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:19.091
At this point, I don't
have time for any mistakes.

00:04:19.157 --> 00:04:22.595
I just need to stay in the game.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.164
 Bladesmiths, to see how
lethal your weapon is,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:30.102
I will deliver multiple slashes
of thrust on this pig carcass.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.070
Steve, you're up first.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:31.870
Are you ready?

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:32.704
 Absolutely.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:33.506
Let's

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.573
 Do this.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.177
 I'm really hoping to hear,
you know, it will kill.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:42.682
[music playing]

00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:53.158
Oh.

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:55.628
 Well, Steve, you
know, I was surprised,

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:58.965
being that you only have a
scale on one side for the handle

00:04:58.998 --> 00:04:59.965
and not on the other.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:01.633
It is a rustic look.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.503
But, nonetheless, it is actually
comfortable to hold on to.

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:07.606
Your tips over there, sharp
enough to cut, easy to thrust

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:11.010
with the bottom, and deliver
a slice at the same time.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:15.248
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.916
 Yeah!

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:17.716
 All right, Nick.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:18.284
You're next.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.218
Are you ready?

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.754
 Oh, yeah.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:25.325
[music playing]

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:38.338
 Well, Nick, your
weapon is very sharp.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:41.707
Grabbing your handle, it
feels smooth with both scales

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.708
in there.

00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:46.412
The angles you have
really lacerate deeply.

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:49.748
And, overall, your
weapon will kill.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:50.749
Good job.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:51.550
 Thank you.

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.018
 Next up is the sharpness test.

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.855
To see how sharp your weapons
are, I will take your weapons

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:59.859
and deliver multiple slashes
and stabs on this ballistic bag.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.728
The bag is outfitted with two
poles, which simulates blocks

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.997
or blows from pole
weapons these knives

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.932
would encounter in battle.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:07.899
Steve, you're up first.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:08.634
You ready?

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.302
 Yes, I am.

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:13.906
[music playing]

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:19.712
[thudding]

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.317
 Well, Steve, the
points are sharp.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.086
They lacerate cleanly.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.187
It feels good in the hand.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.188
I can maneuver.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.256
This, sir, will cut.

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:32.090
 Thank you.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:32.924
 Nick, you're up next.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:33.693
You ready?

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.160
 Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.463
I'm pretty confident mine can
do at least that well, probably

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.665
better, because my
points are more pointier.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:46.772
[music playing]

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:50.410
[thudding]

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:55.714
 Well, Nick, you can see
that it penetrates deep,

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.617
the angles you have them
in, and lacerates out.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.052
They're comfortable in the hand.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.955
And your blades will cut.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:03.656
 Thank you.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.358
 Next up is strength test.

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:06.526
Dave?

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.027
 To test the strength
of your weapons,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.463
we're going to clamp them into
our contraption back here.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.832
Once triggered, a staff will
strike the center section

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:18.036
of each of the blades one time
with a force of 2,000 pounds,

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:20.439
simulating the kind of
attacks these weapons could

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:23.242
historically
encounter in combat.

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:24.376
Steve, are you ready?

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.478
 Yes, I am.

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:28.280
 Three, two, one.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:31.217
[whoosh, clang]

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:34.887
In three, two, one.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.457
[whoosh, clang]

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:41.260
Yeah, well, Steve, I
don't see any damage,

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.728
any rolling of the edge.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.296
So they held up beautifully.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.131
 That's great.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.900
DAVE: Nick?

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:48.901 line:7%
 Just waiting for it.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:49.668 line:7%
Waiting for it.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:53.038
 And one, two, three.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:56.609
[whoosh, clang]

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:58.710
 And it broke the stick.

00:07:58.777 --> 00:07:59.679
[laughs]

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:02.414
DAVE: Three, two, one.

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:05.651
[whoosh, clang]

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:06.518
 Woo!

00:08:06.551 --> 00:08:09.555
[laughs] And it broke
the stick again.

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:10.756
 All right.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:12.058
Well, first off, let's
remember that the test

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.558
wasn't about breaking sticks.

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:15.694
It was more about
how your blade reacts

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.029
to being hit by that stick.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:22.434
There is no damage whatsoever.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.970
This is still a razor blade.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:25.571
Nicely done.

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:26.938
 Thank you.

00:08:27.005 --> 00:08:28.607
 Well, you've both
done commendable work.

00:08:28.673 --> 00:08:30.442
But there can only be
one "Forged in Fire"

00:08:30.475 --> 00:08:32.878
champion in this competition.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:35.848
[music playing]

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:40.419
Nick, congratulations.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.588
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:42.621 --> 00:08:46.158
Steve, your weapons
did not make the cut.

00:08:46.224 --> 00:08:47.593
Dave will explain.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.596
 As Doug said, I really commend
you for doing what you did

00:08:50.662 --> 00:08:52.464
on such a compressed timeline.

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:53.565
 Thank you.

00:08:53.598 --> 00:08:55.167
 In the end, it
came down to the fact

00:08:55.233 --> 00:08:57.303
that the scales aren't quite on.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.737
There's gapping.

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:01.306
There's still some marks from
where you cut the steel open.

00:09:01.373 --> 00:09:02.942
And that's why we're
letting you go.

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.076
 I understand.

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:05.311
 Steve, it's that time.

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:06.946
Please surrender your weapons.

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:07.879
 Congratulations.

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.349
I'm not surprised
at the result. There

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:15.720
is a natural energy that guides
all of us throughout our lives.

00:09:15.787 --> 00:09:18.924
And this is how everything
naturally unfolded.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:22.094
Unfortunately, it didn't
go my way this time.

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:23.229
But I'll be back.

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:26.865
 Nick, congratulations.

00:09:26.898 --> 00:09:28.167
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.536
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:32.471
How do you feel?

00:09:32.537 --> 00:09:34.139
 Pretty darn good.

00:09:34.206 --> 00:09:35.007
[laughter]

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:35.641
 Awesome.

00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:37.442
Good job, brother.

00:09:37.509 --> 00:09:38.777
 That's me.

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:39.945
That's me, the Nick.

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:40.513
That's me.

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:41.914
I won.

00:09:41.947 --> 00:09:44.916
I'm going to hug my
wife when I get home,

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.885
and then I'm going
to hug my kitty-cat.

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:50.256
If any of you other
bladesmiths out there are

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:52.458
thinking about it, I say do it.

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:55.127
Try not to have a cold
when you do it though.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:55.995
[coughs]

00:09:56.561 --> 00:10:00.266
[music playing]

